**`ErrorBoundary.tsx`** — usage:

```tsx
// Basic
<ErrorBoundary>
  <MyComponent />
</ErrorBoundary>

// Custom fallback
<ErrorBoundary fallback={(err, reset) => (
  <div>
    <p>{err.message}</p>
    <button onClick={reset}>Try again</button>
  </div>
)}>
  <MyComponent />
</ErrorBoundary>
```

Key details:
- `getDerivedStateFromError` captures the error into state (triggers fallback render)
- `componentDidCatch` logs `error` + `componentStack` to console
- `reset` clears state — React will re-mount the child tree on next render
- Accepts an optional `fallback` render prop for custom UI; otherwise shows the built-in styled fallback
- Class component is required — hooks can't implement `componentDidCatch`
